+  // Which generation of buffers this pool is currently handing out.
+  //
+  // A pool may discard every buffer it owns and start again, which happens on
+  // GPU context loss. Buffers from an earlier generation are PERMANENTLY
+  // retired: they will never be delivered again. A consumer that keeps
+  // per-buffer state has no other way to learn that, because returning a frame
+  // only makes it available for reuse and says nothing about the buffer being
+  // destroyed.
+  //
+  // Pools that never discard buffers leave this at zero.
+  virtual uint32_t generation() const;
